{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>After my death, when you shall deal corruptly.</b> We do not find that Israel dealt corruptly all the days of Joshua, as it is written (Joshua 24:31): ״ויעבדו העם את ה' כל ימי יהושע וכל ימי הזקנים אשר האריכו ימים אחרי יהושע״ — and the people served HaShem all the days of Joshua and all the days of the elders who lengthened days after Joshua. Rather, from here the Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived that a person's student is as dear to him as his own body, and all the days that Joshua lived it appeared to Moses as though he himself were alive. And this corruption is idol worship, and likewise <b>to provoke Him with the work of your hands</b> alludes to idolatry in the First Temple, for thus the Holy One, blessed be He, informed us explicitly, and He knew this through the holy spirit."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:54.852033554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}